#=====================================================================
# test/diag/tdgbnd.ref
#
# Reference-value data for PROGRAM TDGBND (test/diag/tdgbnd.f).
#
# Routine under test : modern/diag/diaglog.f
# Reference source   : um/MSSG.TXT  (NASTRAN message registry)
#
# DELIVERABLE -- used in Solaris; not executed by Blitzy.
# This file is reference DATA only.  It is NOT a *.f source and is NOT
# matched by the bin/linknas "*.f" build glob, so it is never compiled
# or linked.  It is read/inspected by the unit driver and the test
# harness in the developer's Solaris environment (csh + Sun f77).
#
# Expected verdict   : PASS: TDGBND
#=====================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
#   TDGBND verifies the message-code band reserved for NEW
#   modernization diagnostics emitted through MESAGE by
#   modern/diag/diaglog.f.  The hard constraint (AAP 0.7.2) is:
#   new MESAGE codes live ONLY in the band 9001-9999.  This
#   reference encodes the band bounds, the representative in-band
#   codes the driver exercises, and the registry evidence that
#   justifies the band being free.
#
# RATIONALE (evidence from um/MSSG.TXT)
#   * um/MSSG.TXT registers diagnostic message ids only up to 8015,
#     which is the highest id present in the registry.
#   * A full scan of the registry finds NO ids in the 9001-9999
#     band, so that band is reserved/free for new modernization
#     diagnostics.
#   * um/MSSG.TXT is READ-ONLY for this refactor: new codes are
#     EMITTED at run time by modern/diag/ routines, and are never
#     registered by editing the registry file.
#
# BAND DEFINITION AND REPRESENTATIVE CODES
#   band low  boundary = 9001   (first new-diagnostics code)
#   band high boundary = 9999   (last  new-diagnostics code)
#   guard: low > 8015 (no collision with highest legacy id 8015)
#   representative in-band codes exercised by the driver:
#     9001  ->  low boundary
#     9500  ->  mid band
#     9999  ->  high boundary
#
# CONSISTENCY
#   BAND_LOW / BAND_HIGH and SAMPLE_CODES below MUST match the
#   constants asserted in test/diag/tdgbnd.f (ILOW=9001,
#   IHIGH=9999).  LEGACY_MAX_ID reflects the current um/MSSG.TXT
#   maximum; if the registry ever changes, update this reference
#   and the driver together.
#
#---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-readable key/value lines (whitespace separated, one per
# line).  These are the values the driver and harness parse.
#---------------------------------------------------------------------
BAND_LOW 9001
BAND_HIGH 9999
LEGACY_MAX_ID 8015
SAMPLE_CODES 9001 9500 9999
EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TDGBND
